    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.base16\n\n### Description\n\nThank you for your excellent plugin suite. I was wondering if you could add two extra config parameters for `mini.base16`, specifically:\r\n\r\n- transparent_mode (bool): Support transparency if specified by the terminal emulator (kitty/wezterm for example)\r\n- dim_inactive (bool): Support dimming inactive buffer splits\r\n\r\nFor reference, I added the two options for gruvbox [here](https://github.com/ellisonleao/gruvbox.nvim/pull/149), it would be really nice to support these for mini colorscheme as well :)",
