            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> Disabling the normal group does not seem to be enough. Example screenshot:\r\n\r\nYes, indeed it is not quite enough to achieve 100% transparency, but it is close. Since this issue was closed I've added ['mini.colors'](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/readmes/mini-colors.md) which has the ability to [add transparency](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/f54410c7f866f51711118fd82274043cf731b63d/doc/mini-colors.txt#L409) to any color scheme. So I'd suggest either use it directly (in a form of creating and managing your own color scheme file) or clear highlight groups which bother with not being transparent ([here is a list](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/f54410c7f866f51711118fd82274043cf731b63d/lua/mini/colors.lua#L1244-L1267) from 'mini.colors' implementation).",
